    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model. It's a derived, read-only boolean returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` that is `true` when **any** of the three risk conditions hold, else `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean property to the `Owner` schema (so the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.getRiskFlag()/setRiskFlag()`), documenting the three trigger conditions.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", expression = \"java(riskFlag(owner))\")` plus two methods, following the existing derived-field pattern (`identityKey`, `ownerSegment`, `contactPreference`):\n   - `riskFlag(Owner)` returns true when `possibleDuplicate` is true **OR** `capacityWarning` is true (the city over its soft capacity \u2014 the 40-owner warning threshold) **OR** the email is disposable-adjacent.\n   - `disposableAdjacent(String email)` returns true when the email's domain carries a known disposable provider's name (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) as one of its dot-separated labels without being on the exact blocklist \u2014 e.g. `mailinator.net` or `sub.mailinator.com`. (Exact-blocklist domains like `mailinator.com` are rejected at creation and never stored.)\n\n**Interpretation notes** (the spec's terms are underspecified, so I anchored each to existing codebase concepts):\n- *\"possible duplicate\"* \u2192 the persisted `possibleDuplicate` flag (Cp35 soft-match rule).\n- *\"city over its soft capacity\"* \u2192 the persisted `capacityWarning` flag (city already held 40\u201349 owners at creation \u2014 the soft threshold below the hard limit of 50).\n- *\"disposable-adjacent\"* \u2192 distinct from the hard blocklist; a domain bearing a disposable provider's label on a different TLD/subdomain.\n\nVerification: the target test `Cp58Tests.coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` passes, adjacent tests (Cp35/Cp10/Cp38) pass, and the full suite is green (70/70).",
